# Perception Engine

## Doctrine

- **Perception Engine = product IP** (detectors, IDs, context, catalog, Perception Graph).
- **ModelProvider = implementation detail** — do not hard-code a vendor in domain code.
- Detect → catalog → graph **before** any `ModelProvider.reason` call.
- Outputs are observations/relationships — **not** implementation instructions (**artifact ≠ build order**).

## Modules

- New AI capabilities must register a `PerceptionModule` under `src/perception/modules/`.
- Website review is the first module; audio/image are stubs until authorised.
- Share stable observation IDs, evidence refs, history, PerceptionContext, and graph edges.

## Identity & context

- Observation IDs are human-readable `{surface}.{slug}` — never opaque counters.
- Every observation/edge carries `origin` (`detector`, `version`, `sourceType`).
- Bundles carry `PerceptionContext` (`projectId`, `artifactId`, `version`, `sessionId`).
- Entity layer is reserved (`entityId` optional) — do not invent entity persistence yet.

## Planning / code

- Plans may cite observation IDs (and edge IDs). Implement only with explicit owner approval.
- Do not auto-plan or auto-PR from perception output.
